      "id": 1,
      "text": "Great Mills grew around colonial mills that first appeared in the 17th century, anchoring the community’s agricultural roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/great_mills_maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Patuxent River borders Great Mills, shaping local hydrology and offering access to estuarine environments.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/great_mills_maryland",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Piscataway people originally inhabited the area, using the river for fishing, transport, and trade across the Chesapeake Bay watershed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/great_mills_maryland",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Great Mills is a suburb of Lexington Park and sits near the Naval Air Station Patuxent River, a major U.S. military installation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Mills%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community’s loamy soils, derived from coastal plain sediments, once supported tobacco and now favor sustainable crop cultivation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/great_mills_maryland",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Great Mills is part of Maryland’s oldest counties, with English-speaking settlers establishing farms by the mid‑17th century.",
